Question : 
    Given a non-negative integer s represented as a string, count the number of digits in s that divide the number represented by s.

    A digit is considered valid only if it is non-zero and the number represented by s is divisible by that digit.

    If a digit appears multiple times in s, each occurrence should be counted separately.


Code : 
    class Solution {
        public int divisibleByDigits(String s) {
            // code here
            boolean isDivisible[] = new boolean[10];
            
            for(int d=1; d<=9; d++) {
                int remainder = 0;
                
                for(int i=0; i<s.length(); i++) {
                    remainder = (remainder*10 + (s.charAt(i)-'0'))%d;
                }
                
                if(remainder == 0) {
                    isDivisible[d]  = true;
                }
            }
            
            int count=0;
            for(int i=0; i<s.length(); i++) {
                int d = s.charAt(i)-'0';
                
                if(isDivisible[d]) count++;
            }
            
            return count;
        }
    }



Time Complexity : O(9 × n + n) = O(n)
Space Complexity : O(1)


Explanation : 
    We can convert the s into an integer and perform the rmaining operations but, 
    after converting it into, we can store in a int variable as the constraints say 1 ≤ s.size() ≤ 106

    So we should to use BigInteger which gives
    Time: O(n × d), where n is the number of digits and d is the cost of dividing the BigInteger by a single digit.
S   pace: O(n) for storing the BigInteger.

    A better approach is
        We don't convert s into an integer. 

        All digits lie in the range 0 and 9.
        So we create a 10 digit array(boolean) which tells that a number divides the s or not.

        We go from 1 to 9 digits
        And for every digit, we divide the s by the digit by performing literal divison.
        remainder = (remainder*10 + (s.charAt(i)-'0'))%d;

        if remainder becomes 0, we mark the idx of the array true.

        In this way the array contains all 9 digits info(i.e. whether they can divide the s or not).

        Finally, we again traverse on s, and for every character in s, we convert it into int and 
        we check in the array at that difits idx, if it is true count++.

        We ignore 0, because num/0 = 0

        Finally we return count;